# WATCHING A FALL, FRAME BY FRAME.
#
# The point is that the pictures are placed by TICK, not by keyboard input: the
# character is set walking once, and every snapshot after that is the simulation
# advanced a known amount. Add a `step`/`snap` pair anywhere and you get another
# frame of the same fall — remove one and nothing else moves.
#
# ⚠ rate 0 is what makes them comparable. At any other rate the wall clock also
# advances ticks between commands, so "ten ticks later" is only approximately ten.

rate 0
at 0 0 0

echo --- a hill to fall off
verb raise
step 5
verb raise
step 5
verb raise
step 5
save fallworld

echo --- stand on it and walk over the edge
at 15 0 0
step 30
snap fall-00

keys 1
step 20
snap fall-01
step 10
snap fall-02
step 10
snap fall-03
step 10
snap fall-04
step 20
snap fall-05
keys 0
step 20
snap fall-06
